The error you're encountering is due to the limitation of available PCI slots when hot-plugging devices in KubeVirt. The maximum number of PCI slots available for a virtual machine in KubeVirt is 32, which includes slots used by other devices such as disks and guest agents <sup>[[1]](https://kubevirt.io/user-guide/network/hotplug_interfaces)</sup>.

To work around this limitation, you can use a `virtio-scsi` controller, which allows for hotplugging of disks using a `scsi` bus. This method supports over 4 million disks, thus overcoming the constraints of the 32 PCI slots <sup>[[2]](https://kubevirt.io/user-guide/operations/hotplug_volumes)</sup>. You can modify your VirtualMachineInstance manifest to use a `scsi` bus for the disks you want to hotplug. This should help you successfully attach more than four data disks to your virtual machine.


